# Fragua

AI-native PCB design tool. One Go binary: a script API for you, a live browser UI for the
human at <http://127.0.0.1:7878/ui/>.

## Launch

Bare `fragua` prints help and exits — always use a subcommand:

```sh
fragua mcp board.fragua   # MCP on stdio + HTTP API + UI
fragua run board.fragua   # HTTP API + UI only
```

## Drive it

Use the `fragua_*` MCP tools if configured, otherwise HTTP:

```sh
curl -s http://127.0.0.1:7878/help                  # full verb reference
curl -s 'http://127.0.0.1:7878/help?verb=route'     # one verb
curl -s http://127.0.0.1:7878/script -H 'content-type: application/json' \
  -d '{"script":"outline 30 20\nstatus"}'
```

Script is line-oriented; indented lines continue a `sym`/`lib` block. **Execution stops at
the first failing line.** Results are `ok <verb>: …` or `error line <n> <verb>: …`.

Do not guess argument names — read `/help?verb=<verb>` first.

## Recipe

```text
outline 30 20 radius=2
fab-rules jlcpcb                 # set BEFORE routing
class ground pour=both

sym U1 ic key=esp32_s3_zero      # kinds: ic resistor capacitor inductor led diode
  pin 1 L GND role=power_in
  pin 2 R IO1 role=bidir
sym C1 capacitor key=c_0603
net GND U1.GND C1.2 class=ground
nc U1.IO9                        # unused pins, or ERC calls them floating
erc                              # iterate to 0 errors

list-lib                         # 70+ footprints exist; look before authoring with `lib`
palette U1 esp32_s3_zero         # binds the footprint — does NOT place it
place U1 15 10                   # anchor what matters
edge-place J1 bottom             # connectors
auto-place seed=42               # seats the unplaced (C1) and arranges them

route max_seconds=120            # re-run: it only attacks open nets
auto-pour
stitch
drc
pack fab=jlcpcb out=/tmp
save /abs/path/board.fragua
```

## Rules

- `palette` binds a footprint; `place` / `place-legal` / `edge-place` the parts whose
  position matters. `auto-place` seats every bound-but-unplaced part itself.
- Anchor ICs and connectors before `auto-place`, or passives scatter from their IC.
- `route: N/M nets ok` — re-run while `N` improves. When it plateaus, the geometry is
  blocking; more seconds will not help. Add area, move a part, or `layer add`.
- `erc`/`drc` return counts, not locations. Errors must be 0. See where via the UI or
  `screenshot`.
- `pack` only refuses on **ERC** errors; it will pack a DRC-dirty board and report
  `drc_err=N`. Never ship that silently.
- Re-routing order: `clear-pour` → `route` → `auto-pour` → `stitch`.
- Memory-only sessions lose everything: `save /abs/path.fragua` early.
- Budgets: `route max_seconds=90..180`, always pass `auto-place seed=N`.

When the router plateaus or a design decision is ambiguous, ask the human — they are
watching the UI and can drag a part or relax a constraint.
